{"c":[{"id":"1e0ecf55978bf1c4","sum":"Dead shim: ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP (EACCES/ESTALE stay). Owner rules in systemPatterns, else ask. Local-path mkts load from source; CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR moves plugins. Hooks expand ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}; paths quoted. Cron has PATH+STOCKROOM_HOME. Archive copy: git init for reuse lint.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ff4a86710809ce02","sum":"Dead shim: ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP; EACCES/ESTALE stay. Owner: claude if installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the root, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask. Local-path mkts load from source. orphan=version-dir+.orphaned_at. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/..._CACHE_DIR move plugins.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c1e11d92dfb9eca2","sum":"ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP=dead;EACCES/ESTALE stay. Claude ask; Cursor=CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT. installed_plugins.json beside cache/=cache copy not checkout; dir-mkt. --plugin-dir/synced none. orphan=version-dir+.orphaned_at. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR+CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fea602b5005e86e1","sum":"shim _alive is dead only on ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP. EACCES/ESTALE stay alive, so rectify leaves it. Path.is_file raises before 3.14 and returns False from 3.14. Claude-only fixes must not question Cursor users. sr-initialize asks only in Claude Code; Cursor uses CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T215531Z-cabd5aa56838fc34","text":"shim _alive: only ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP mean a baked engine is dead; other stat errors (EACCES, ESTALE) count as alive, so rectify leaves it. Do not use Path.is_file: it raises those before Python 3.14 and returns False from 3.14.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261016T222048Z-5c4cd091dd70b15f","text":"Design rule (operator, 2026-10-16): fixes for Claude Code-only problems must not add questions for Cursor users. sr-initialize asks the user only in Claude Code; Cursor keeps its own evidence (CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc126cfe9aa69545","sum":"installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists only the cache copy, never the checkout (dir-marketplace too). --plugin-dir and synced copies: none; orphans keep version-dir plus .orphaned_at. Cursor: no record. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move the plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T223043Z-086a0d75fd95fd94","text":"Claude Code proves an install by its record, not its folder: installed_plugins.json in the plugins root (beside cache/) lists each installPath; --plugin-dir (@inline) and synced copies have none; orphans keep a version-named folder plus .orphaned_at. Cursor has no such record.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T010120Z-43ea3096fec682fc","text":"Claude Code copies even directory-marketplace plugins (source ./ too) into <plugins root>/cache/<mkt>/<plugin>/<version>; installed_plugins.json there records only that copy, never the checkout. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR both move the plugins root.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ea3fa59ce852af66","sum":"Owner outside default plugin dirs: claude if installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT), else none. Local-path marketplaces load from source, not installPath. ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}=<plugins root>/data/<id>; read paths via quoted heredoc.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0759e81a67d39207","sum":"Outside default plugin folders, claude means installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact plugin root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT); else no owner. A local-path marketplace caches and records a relative-path plugin, but loads it from the source folder, not installPath.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T012636Z-cb621eb5522291ae","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: an install-shaped copy outside the default plugins folders is claude when installed_plugins.json beside its cache/ holds the quoted exact plugin root (grep -qF), checked before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT; else no owner. Supersedes the round-1 owner-rule note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T014809Z-c4ddf9bb24e2c594","text":"Correction: relative-path plugins in a local-path Claude Code marketplace get a cache entry and an install record, but load in place from the source folder (claude plugin list --json readFromFolder). installPath is not always the folder a plugin loads from.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"477b2af74f8da1f7","sum":"CC 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in skill text: <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline (--plugin-dir) or stockroom-<marketplace>; 'inline' reserved. SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" re-parses the pasted path; quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r is safe.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135741Z-0a0d4ec0ff68165a","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in plugin skill text (typed or model-invoked, prose or fence): <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline for --plugin-dir, stockroom-<marketplace> for installs. Marketplace name 'inline' is reserved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T135751Z-db7b381ea6596dc0","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" lets the shell re-parse the pasted path ($x, backtick, $(), quote pairs change it or run commands; a lone \" is a syntax error). A quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r passed all cases in dash/bash/busybox.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8f544ca9fb1ae138","sum":"Hooks expand ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}; Step 2 reads pasted paths via quoted heredoc; owner rules in systemPatterns. Shell and printed paths quoted. Cron/launchd carry PATH+STOCKROOM_HOME. Git-archive engine copy: git init+add -A for reuse lint. Torch fail: ensure-env if freeze.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3ce3ee33dcc4f281","sum":"Hooks expand \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" from env; skill text is pasted raw, so Step 2 reads paths via quoted heredoc. Owner: claude if <root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask. Shell paths quoted.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"def92aca321a0958","sum":"CC 2.1.302 hooks expand \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" from env (safe); skill text is pasted raw. sr-initialize owner: default plugin dirs by path; else claude if <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135752Z-8f76ec9421650d2c","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 shell-form hooks: \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" is expanded by the shell from the env, not pasted as text (a $ in the path survives), so hooks/claude-hooks.json is safe from path re-parsing. Skill text is pasted raw.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T143558Z-05746a642d0f531d","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 owner (round 3): default plugins dirs by path; elsewhere a cache-shaped copy is claude if Claude's data dir is <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if data dir is stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ed3458896fa1f4ac","sum":"sr-initialize Step 2 reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r); a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Paths in shell text are quoted (shlex.quote, Makefile \"...\"): space and ' work; $, backtick, \", \\, % out of scope.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T143616Z-2bbea48021b44381","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 now reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} and ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r), so the shell never parses the pasted paths and no env var stands in; a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Supersedes the SKILL_DIR=\"...\" note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T171632Z-1ff8e252c90ac5da","text":"Every path stockroom writes into shell text is quoted: Step 2 heredoc, shim and scheduler entries via shlex.quote, Makefile recipes via double quotes. A space or ' must work; rarer chars ($, backtick, \", \\, %) are out of scope (2026-10-18).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f2b8fe2f4481d376","sum":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and STOCKROOM_HOME; schedule status shows up-to-date and entry home; Step 8 offers re-install. Printed commands quote paths too. A git-archive engine copy needs git init + add -A for reuse lint. Torch fail: ensure-env if freeze, else pip.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6b46287778b27850","sum":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and STOCKROOM_HOME (no profile); 'schedule status' shows up-to-date: and entry home:, and Step 8 offers re-install. Path quoting covers printed commands too (doctor smoke remedy, localdev hint): audit messages, not only shell code.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261018T171639Z-5cb80849a2e584b6","text":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and the resolved STOCKROOM_HOME (no shell profile is loaded); 'schedule status' prints up-to-date: and entry home:, and sr-initialize Step 8 offers a consented re-install of a stale entry.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T203924Z-9f05cc054dcdf6ff","text":"Path quoting also covers commands stockroom prints for someone to run (doctor smoke's torch remedy, localdev.sh's --plugin-dir hint). When auditing shell text, search printed messages too, not only code that runs a shell.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8039db218a133a07","sum":"Engine suite from a git-archive copy: test_reuse_lint_passes fails once coverage-engine's sync made the copy's .venv; git init + git add -A avoids it. semantic/embed exit 1 with one torch line: ensure-env if a usable freeze exists, else the quoted pip line.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261018T211547Z-7e6ede0556b999df","text":"Engine suite from a git-archive copy (empty .git marker): test_reuse_lint_passes fails whenever make coverage-engine's sync has created the copy's skills/sr-search/.venv first; git init plus git add -A in the copy avoids it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261020T175250Z-aa5758b35ed49d8e","text":"semantic and embed exit 1 with one torch line: ensure-env when a usable freeze exists, else the quoted pip line; an encoder failure after import says re-run sr-initialize, not ensure-env.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"bc5f67e1f2368b8f","sum":"Releases stand alone; v0.1.0-v2.1.3 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4 (wild: v1.0.0+, schema 0-8, rows at 4+). 2.0 files v2.0.0+; zstd fails on v1.0.0. Issue 147 copy chain is durable. Doctor never writes except 'doctor fix <name>'. Power loss must not empty the warehouse.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fc17f5508263ee34","sum":"Releases stand alone; v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4: wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8. 2.0 files are v2.0.0+, unopenable before 2.0. 2.0 zstd: BinderException on v1.0.0. Issue 147 chain: short-lived, own module, data-safe. embed/semantic heal torch from the freeze.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a16996d817dbf8d7","sum":"semantic/embed heal torch once from a hashed freeze, else name sr-initialize; nightly: ensure-env; ingest && embed. Issue 147 chain is short-lived (~5-6 installs), own module, data-safe. DuckDB 2.0 (LTS to Oct 2027): new files v2.0.0+, unreadable before 2.0.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2344b5030265f7ee","sum":"semantic/embed restore torch once from a usable hashed freeze and retry; else say re-run sr-initialize. doctor smoke is report-only. Nightly payload: (date; stockroom shim ensure-env; stockroom ingest && stockroom embed): a failed heal still ingests; failed ingest skips embed.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261020T193116Z-270eb1650c4e7f96","text":"semantic and embed restore torch once from a usable hashed freeze and retry; no freeze, a failed restore, or any other encoder failure says re-run sr-initialize. doctor smoke stays report-only and still names ensure-env when a freeze exists.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261020T205704Z-a2498a1e20047fe3","text":"Nightly cron and launchd payload is (date; stockroom shim ensure-env; stockroom ingest && stockroom embed). A failed heal still ingests; a failed ingest still skips embed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1046806e8c5186a7","sum":"Issue 147 migration chain (copy, check, swap) is short-lived (~5-6 installs, a month or two), own module, reliable not bulletproof; data-safety holds. DuckDB 2.0.0 (LTS to Oct 2027; 1.5 to Mar 2027): suite passes; new files are v2.0.0+, unreadable before 2.0.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T145418Z-a7061b3a1a0c5bbf","text":"Issue 147 storage migration chain (verified copy, session-start check, swap) is short-lived: about 5-6 installs, kept a month or two, then removed. Build it reliable, not bulletproof; data-safety rules still hold. Keep it in its own module.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T155046Z-35a2088124b6c3aa","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 (2026-10-21, LTS to Oct 2027; 1.5 to Mar 2027): engine suite passes unchanged (uv --with overlay), vss loads, HNSW still used (EXPLAIN prints 'Hnsw Index Scan', not HNSW_INDEX_SCAN). New files are v2.0.0+ by default; DuckDB before 2.0 cannot read them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3969d97bee49fe6a","sum":"Releases stand alone; v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8 (tests make v1.0.0 on purpose). 1.5.4 replays a v1.0.0+ file a killed 2.0.0 writer left, and cannot open v2.0.0+. 2.0.0 zstd clause: BinderException on v1.0.0, ZSTD at v1.2.0+.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1f960dec0850b21e","sum":"Releases stand alone (users skip them); v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8; old-format tests create v1.0.0 on purpose. 1.5.4 opens and replays a v1.0.0+ file a killed 2.0.0 writer left; only v2.0.0+ files are unreadable.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T160004Z-0474312fdfee4cb0","text":"Every stockroom release must stand alone: users skip releases. Releases v0.1.0-v2.1.2 all pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so warehouses in the wild are v1.0.0+ at schema 1-8. Under DuckDB 2.0, tests that need an old-format file must create it at storage v1.0.0 on purpose.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T161737Z-639a1a68a7083e6a","text":"Measured 2026-10-21: DuckDB 1.5.4 opens (ro and rw) a v1.0.0+ file a crashed DuckDB 2.0.0 writer left with a wal, plain or vss HNSW-indexed, and replays all rows; the wal matches a 1.5.4 writer's in size. Only files 2.0 creates (v2.0.0+) are unreadable before 2.0.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c27c79ce59ec8d2","sum":"DuckDB 2.0.0: USING COMPRESSION zstd raises BinderException on v1.0.0 storage (1.5.4 ignores it); v1.2.0+ gives ZSTD, so zstd in 0001 breaks v1.0.0 fixtures. 2.0.0 wal replay into an HNSW index breaks it (InternalException or hang); DROP+CREATE+CHECKPOINT repairs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T164029Z-dd6c62dffb711e78","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 raises BinderException for USING COMPRESSION zstd at storage v1.0.0 (1.5.4 stored it uncompressed silently); v1.2.0+ storage gives ZSTD. A zstd clause in 0001 breaks a schema-0 v1.0.0+ file and old-format test fixtures built from current 0001.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T170926Z-f865c4bcdda86174","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 bug: replaying a wal holding inserts into an HNSW-indexed table (killed 1.5.4 or 2.0 writer) breaks the index: query, delete, insert raise InternalException (flat or constant vector) or hang. 1.5.4 replays fine. DROP INDEX, CREATE INDEX, CHECKPOINT repairs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"53c4596b9c089045","sum":"Doctor probe/smoke never write; writes only via 'stockroom doctor fix <name>' (operator 2026-10-21). ~5 installs; tune for a finished nightly embed; power loss must not empty the warehouse. HNSW re-add: deletes with index up leak; drop, delete, recreate once, checkpoint.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd4ef639b21c204f","sum":"Operator 2026-10-21: discoverable doctor commands (probe, smoke) never write; writes only via 'stockroom doctor fix <name>'. About five installs, nightly embed, rollout takes days; tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page, not an empty warehouse.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ed5a4442c6ce5e9c","sum":"Doctor rule (operator, 2026-10-21): discoverable doctor commands (probe, smoke) never write; writes only via 'stockroom doctor fix <name>'. DuckDB 2.0.0 vss HNSW replay bug: auto-checkpoint folds the wal, index misses replayed rows; moot once index and vss were dropped.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T174235Z-774be06df86dea8f","text":"stockroom doctor rule (operator, 2026-10-21): any discoverable doctor command (probe, smoke) never writes. Every doctor write sits behind 'stockroom doctor fix <name>' and runs only when named. First fix planned: 'doctor fix hnsw-wal' for the DuckDB 2.0.0 HNSW replay bug.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T175900Z-bd6ed7dba4d68c72","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 replay bug goes silent: other writers succeed, the wal grows, and past checkpoint_threshold (16 MiB) the auto-checkpoint folds it. Then the HNSW index silently lacks the replayed rows (pragma_hnsw_index_info count < count(*)); top-k skips them. A rebuild fixes it.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3315768ae2a907e4","sum":"Operator 2026-10-21: about five installs, nightly embed, rollout takes days; tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page and must not empty the warehouse. The HNSW doctor-only fold check and 'doctor fix hnsw-rebuild' went with the dropped index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T191821Z-1972e75cf1dd3323","text":"Operator 2026-10-21: silent HNSW fold is doctor-only, plus an index-coverage check. No repair on reconnect. The fix command is doctor fix hnsw-rebuild.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T193821Z-1b68223f17357c6b","text":"Operator 2026-10-21: about five installs, nightly embed, rollout is days. Tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page. It must not empty the warehouse. HNSW drops only around inserts.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2f50c65a5d0f58b3","sum":"HNSW re-add (2026-10-21, 1.5.4, 2.0.0): index down until all embedding deletes run, then one recreate. Delete with index up leaks one at checkpoint/close (no-match does not); recreate between deletes leaks. No checkpoint while down. Drop, delete, recreate, checkpoint stays flat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"594740d627151f97","sum":"HNSW, for any later re-add (2026-10-21, DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0): deleting embeddings rows with the index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close; a no-match delete does not. Drop index, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps used blocks flat.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T200533Z-dc75d974ecb1c63f","text":"2026-10-21: deleting embeddings rows with the HNSW index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close, on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. A no-match delete does not. The drop covers those deletes, not only inserts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T202433Z-25b36bcacf2f9117","text":"2026-10-21 eleventh L4 preflight PASS WITH ADVISORY. Drop, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps HNSW used blocks flat on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Advisories unadopted: checkpoint while the index is down; ingest keeps the index down for the whole process.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a03e92dc6ad2d6f7","sum":"HNSW write rules, for any later re-add (operator 2026-10-21): keep the index down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then recreate once (a recreate between deletes leaks a copy); no checkpoint while it is down. Growth tests assert used blocks each cycle.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T211831Z-daa0544e233ebf48","text":"Growth test asserts used blocks or a high-water of one index over the start, every cycle. No checkpoint while the HNSW index is down; the next cycle reclaims that free copy. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T213401Z-eb3da00d50779e55","text":"HNSW stays down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then one recreate. A recreate between two deletes leaks a used copy on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
